descriptionByLocale.en:
Night watch for the area "La Côte" CDI - Participation rate to be agreed, 60% to 100%

Deployed at several sites, the Lavigny Institution consists of a neurological hospital with outpatient consultations at two sites, two departments for adults with disabilities, with an intellectual disability with a physical problem, a specialized school and a workshop and vocational training sector respectively.

The socio-educational housing department is recruiting. If you want to work in interdisciplinarity around strong values that are:

Benevolence, fairness, respect and responsibility in a collaborative managerial approach.

You can join our educational teams.
We are looking for one:

Night watch for the area "La Côte" CDI - Participation rates to be agreed

At the Institution of Lavigny, we accompany adults with disabilities on a daily basis, particularly with an intellectual disability and/or a polydisability.
The night watchman is in charge of active evening and night surveillance from Monday to Sunday from 9:45 to 7:15.
Your Mission

We are looking for a night watchman to accompany the people welcomed in the acts related to daily life in the evening and at night, according to the concept of accompaniment for people with disabilities. It ensures the continuity of this support in line with institutional, sector, group and individual projects. The objective is to actively monitor those welcomed on night rest times.
Your main responsibilities

• Accompany guests in the evening and at night;

• Ensure the physical and psychological comfort and security of the person being received;

• Monitoring individual projects;

• Collaborate in partnership with the members of the day team.
Your profile

• Red Cross Certification;

• Social skills;

• Ability to work independently and take initiatives;

• Meaning of observation and organization;

• Aisance in oral and written communication;

• Ability to experience empathy, to question oneself, to have a global vision.
We offer

• Working conditions agreed by the Commission for the Parapublic Social Sector;

• A salary in line with the function and in line with the scales of the CTCs in the Vaudian parapublic sector, with mobility-related benefits (parking, participation in public transport costs);

• In-service training and specialized supervision (including TSA and challenge behaviour), internal mobility, possible funding of diplomas and certifications;

• A business restaurant offering varied meals at preferential rates, in a pleasant business environment conducive to exchanges;

• The possibility of part-time work for an optimal balance between work and private life.
Start-up: as soon as possible or to be agreed
Deadline for application: 22 November 2026
Information: Mr. Cyril Lacour, Area Manager, 021 821 45 45

Want a new challenge? Send your complete dossier (motivation letter, CV, work certificates and diplomas) exclusively to Write an email - we are waiting for your application!

